entQa","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/AllCliques\/flatMap(_:)-6afzx","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/allcliques\/flatmap(_:)-6afzx","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/AllCliques":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AllCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AllCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AllCliques","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/allcliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/AllCliques","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph whose size is in a range, once each, lazily,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order (by vertex index). The order is by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then depth first, each clique followed by its extensions by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"later vertices in ascending index. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating again gives the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d) bitset words per clique for degeneracy d."}]}}}